WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:12.980
The greatest lecture or sermon you will give
is your example. What you do will matter far

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:20.410
more than what you say. As my grandfather
often said, "We were duty-bound to do the

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:29.359
right thing, to do unto others as we would
have them do unto us." In a sense, they were

00:00:29.359 --> 00:00:38.420
teaching us that what we wanted to do did
not define what was right, rather, what was

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:46.829
right defined what we were required to do
and what we were permitted to do. At the risk

00:00:46.829 --> 00:00:53.870
of understating what is necessary to preserve
liberty and our form of government, I think

00:00:53.870 --> 00:01:00.379
more and more that it depends on good citizens
discharging their daily duties and their daily

00:01:00.379 --> 00:01:08.500
obligations. Some of you will most assuredly
be called upon to do the very hard things

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:14.920
to preserve liberty, perhaps even given the
last full measure, but all of you will be

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:22.619
called upon to provide that firm foundation
of citizenship by carrying out your obligations

00:01:22.619 --> 00:01:30.810
in much the way that those around you did
and so many did during my youth. You are to

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:38.610
be the example to others that they were to
you. The very existence of Hillsdale connotes

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:46.619
independence. It understands that liberty
is an antecedent of government, not a benefit

00:01:46.619 --> 00:01:54.880
from government. Do not hide your faith and
your beliefs under a bushel basket especially

00:01:54.880 --> 00:02:01.360
in this world that seems to have gone mad
with political correctness. I admit to being

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:10.619
unapologetically Catholic, unapologetically
patriotic, and unapologetically a constitutionalist.

00:02:10.619 --> 00:02:17.850
After the constitutional convention in Philadelphia,
Benjamin Franklin remarked when asked what

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:25.269
they had done that they had given us a republic
if we can keep it. Are we content to let others

00:02:25.269 --> 00:02:34.699
do the work, to let a few give the last full
measure for liberty while we consume the benefits?

00:02:34.699 --> 00:02:43.790
If so, perhaps one day, we will run out of
other people's sacrifice and courage, and

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:53.660
perhaps we will run out of courageous people
willing to make the sacrifice, but this is

00:02:53.660 --> 00:03:01.919
Hillsdale College, and you are special, that
shining city on a hill. Hillsdale is a trustee

00:03:01.919 --> 00:03:10.620
of the heritage that finds its clearest expression
in the American experiment of self-government

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:19.299
under law. You are men and women of Hillsdale
College, a school that has stood fast on its

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:29.630
principles and its traditions at great sacrifice
and great cost. You are men and women of Hillsdale,

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:36.220
steeped in the best traditions and principles
of our great nation.

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:42.350
If you don't lead by example, who will? I
have every faith that you will be the beacon

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:50.570
of light for others to follow, that city on
a hill that cannot be hidden. May God bless

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:56.490
each of you now and throughout your lives
and may God bless America. Thank you.

